      "message": "FYI, this is not really a comment for this CL, but I\u0027ve been considering adding a IHidlInterface type to represent the HIDL \"interface\" keyword. This type would have methods to retrieve the interface name, version as well as a way to get the transport object (eg an IBinder). This would allow clients to pass \"any HIDL interface\", and the remote could use the name/version information to convert it back to the correct object.\n\nReason: camera guys have\nopen(ICameraDevice@1.0 device);\nopen_2x(ICameraDevice@2.0 device);\nopen_3x(ICameraDevice@3.0 device);\n\nideally they want\n\nopen(interface device);\nor\nopen(ICameraDevice@* device);\n\nit removes type-safety from the interface, but it\u0027s probably a net-positive in code simplicity.",
